   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "para",
   "marker": "ip",
   "content": [
    "A large portion of the document is poetry, with some narrative portions also included. Unlike English poetry which can often focus on rhyme, Hebrew poetry often includes parallelism where the same thought is repeated or extended using different words. The ",
    {
     "type": "char",
     "marker": "em",
     "content": [
      "OET Readers’ Version"
     ]
    },
    " tries to assist the reader by starting the second line in a parallel set with the symbol ",
    {
